        "eventMetadata": {
          "context_description": "Xi Jinping maintains firm institutional control as paramount leader through his roles as CCP General Secretary, Central Military Commission chairman, and president, with no term limits in place since the 2018 constitutional changes. Recent developments, including July 2026 reporting on preparations for a fourth term at the 2027 party congress and the absence of visible successors or factional challenges in the Politburo, reinforce expectations of continuity into at least 2028. Military leadership adjustments and elite promotions have aligned with his authority rather than undermining it, while broader surveillance and party structures limit organized opposition. Trader consensus at 95.5% for \"No\" reflects these structural barriers and the low base rate of sudden removals for incumbents in this system. Even so, unforeseen events such as a severe health crisis or rapid elite realignment amid economic pressures could still shift outcomes before the end of 2026.",
          "context_requires_regen": false,
