        "eventMetadata": {
          "context_description": "The Democratic field for the 2028 presidential nomination remains fragmented, with no candidate exceeding 21 percent in current trader pricing as Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez leads narrowly at 20.1 percent ahead of Gavin Newsom and Jon Ossoff. Recent approval of the DNC primary calendar, placing South Carolina first followed by Nevada and other diverse states, has highlighted the importance of early support among Black, Latino, and union voters without yet producing consolidation. New Hampshire polling gains for Ocasio-Cortez, combined with Newsom's softer positioning amid California governance scrutiny and Ossoff's appeal as a battleground Senate winner, have kept the top tier tightly bunched. Absence of formal announcements, 2026 midterm outcomes, and bloc-specific endorsements could widen gaps among governors, senators, and House members ahead of formal contests.",
